:\"Change PD ({{pd}}mm)\",\"fittingbox.changePd\":\"Change PD ({0}mm)\",\"header.skipToMain.text\":\"SKIP TO MAIN CONTENT\",\"header.skipToChat.text\":\"SKIP TO CHAT BUTTON\",\"plp.appliedFilters.clearFilters\":\"Clear filters\",\"header.skipToFilter.text\":\"SKIP TO FILTER\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.error.values.between\":\"Enter values between {{min}}{{unit}} and {{max}}{{unit}}\",\"plp.search.sortAndFilter\":\"Filter \u0026 Sort\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize.tooltip.button\":\"Redo your size measurement\",\"header.skipToFooter.text\":\"SKIP TO FOOTER\",\"plp.filterbox.filters\":\"Filters\",\"plp.filter.pd.right\":\"Right\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.to\":\"to\",\"plp.filterbox.seeResultsCount\":\"See results ({{count}})\",\"plp.filterbox.showResults\":\"Show results\",\"global.seeCoupons.label\":\"See Coupons\",\"plp.filter.pd.left\":\"Left\",\"plp.filter.pd.oneNumber\":\"One number\",\"plp.filterbox.hideFilters\":\"Hide Filters\",\"plp.filter.pd.findMyPD\":\"Find my PD\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize.modal.button\":\"Find {{frameSize}} Size Frames\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.error.first.less.than.second\":\"First value must be less than second value\",\"plp.filter.pd.select\":\"Select\",\"plp.filter.pd.twoNumbers\":\"Two numbers\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.unit\":\"mm\",\"global.pdp.cta.enterPrescription\":\"Enter Prescription\",\"pdp.bundle.tintOnly.lensType\":\"Lens type\",\"plp.title.relatedProducts\":\"Related Products\",\"global.shop.tag\":\"Frames\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findMySize\":\"Find my size\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize.kids.tooltip.title\":\"Lens Width: {{width}}\",\"fittingBox.modal.frames.label\":\"Frames\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize.adults.tooltip.content\":\"Your frame width measurement typically fits our {{measurement}} size frames.\",\"global.fittingbox.fittingBoxAthleisureTintMapping\":\"$46\",\"fittingBox.modal.lenses.label\":\"Lenses\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findMySizeLabel\":\"Not sure?\",\"account.orderItem.orderFAQItems\":\"$47\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize.kids.tooltip.content\":\"Your lens width measurement typically fits our {{measurement}} size frames.\",\"global.productTile.similarFrames.label\":\"See similar frames\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize.adults.tooltip.title\":\"Frame Width: {{width}}\",\"global.fittingbox.fittingBoxTintMapping\":\"$48\",\"account.orderCard.orderSummaryTotal\":\"Total (USD)\",\"account.orderCard.printButtonText\":\"Print FSA Receipt\",\"account.dashboard.recentOrders.btn.printFSAHSAReceipt\":\"Print FSA Receipt\",\"sign.in.flag.altText\":\"Shop Zenni Optical USA\",\"global.fittingbox.fittingBoxPremiumTintMapping\":\"$49\",\"plp.filter.frameSizes.teenSize.label\":\"Teen Size\",\"global.i18n.message.one\":\"one\",\"plp.filter.frameWidth.tooltipContent.kids\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"frame-width-tooltip-content\\\"\u003e\\n  \u003cp class=\\\"sub-title\\\"\u003eBased on lens width\u003c/p\u003e\\n  \u003cp\u003e\\n    \u003cimg src=\\\"/marketing/productList/Lens-width-Kids-PLP-tooltip.png\\\" alt=\\\"lens width\\\"\u003e\\n  \u003c/p\u003e\\n  \u003cp class=\\\"age-category\\\"\u003eKids\u003c/p\u003e\\n  \u003cdiv class=\\\"sizes-content\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eAges 0-3\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e35 - 40 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eAges 4-6\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e41 - 45 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eAges 7-9\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e46 - 48 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eAges 10-13\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e49 - 58 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n  \u003c/div\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.tint.eyeqidguard\":\"EyeQLenz™\",\"global.badges.config\":\"$4a\",\"global.bnpl.disclosures\":\"$4b\",\"plp.filter.frameWidth.tooltipContent.adult\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"frame-width-tooltip-content\\\"\u003e\\n  \u003cp class=\\\"sub-title\\\"\u003eBased on frame width\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n    \u003cimg src=\\\"/marketing/productList/Frame-width-Adult-PLP-tooltip.svg\\\" alt=\\\"frame width\\\"\u003e\\n  \u003c/p\u003e\\n  \u003cp class=\\\"age-category\\\"\u003eAdults\u003c/p\u003e\\n  \u003cdiv class=\\\"sizes-content\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eXS\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e110 - 118 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eS\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e119 - 125 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eM\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e126 - 132 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eL\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e133 - 140 mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-item\\\"\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-label\\\"\u003eXL\u003c/div\u003e\\n      \u003cdiv class=\\\"size-desc\\\"\u003e141+ mm\u003c/div\u003e\\n    \u003c/div\u003e\\n  \u003c/div\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\\n\",\"global.header.messageRibbon.previousMessage\":\"Previous message\",\"global.header.messageRibbon.nextMessage\":\"Next message\",\"global.search.searchPlaceholder\":\"Search glasses\",\"pdp.tint.fashion.desc\":\"(Lighter tints for casual sports or indoors)\",\"header.help.content\":\"[\\n        {\\n            \\\"icon\\\": \\\"\u003ci class=\\\\\\\"fas fa-truck font-medium\\\\\\\"\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\\\",\\n            \\\"link\\\": \\\"/myAccount/myOrders\\\",\\n            \\\"anonymousLink\\\": \\\"/trackOrder\\\",\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Track my order\\\",\\n            \\\"className\\\": \\\"md:!tw-hidden\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"link\\\": \\\"/c/faq\\\",\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"FAQ\\\",\\n            \\\"target\\\": \\\"__blank\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"link\\\": \\\"/c/how-to\\\",\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"How to’s\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"link\\\": \\\"/measuring-pd-infographic\\\",\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Measure your pupillary distance - PD\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"link\\\": \\\"/help\\\",\\n            \\\"role\\\": \\\"button\\\",\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Help center\\\"\\n        }\\n    ]\",\"global.predefinedUUID\":\"ffa9622a-4246-4b71-8873-b67402cb4310\",\"plp.productList.columnControl\":\"View by columns of\",\"pdp.polarized.price.label.from\":\"from\",\"plp.filter.frameSize.findYourSize\":\"Find your size\",\"plp.filterbox.clearAll\":\"Clear all\",\"plp.filter.frameSizes.viewLess\":\"View less\",\"plp.filter.frameSizes.viewMore\":\"View more\",\"global.normalAnchor.play\":\"Resume carousel animation\",\"plp.NewPLPBackTop.backTop\":\"Scroll back to top\",\"pdp.relatedSku.successMessage\":\"Added to cart\",\"global.product.size.related.oversize\":\"Wide Lenses\",\"pdp.reviews.usage\":\"Usage\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.pd\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"tw-gap-10 tw-flex tw-flex-col\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cp class=\\\"p1\\\"\u003ePupillary Distance (PD) is the distance, in millimeters, between the center of one pupil to the center of the\\n        other. The PD is needed to manufacture your eyeglasses because it determines the exact optical center of the\\n        lens, which is the point where you look through the lens. PD is especially important for manufacturing\\n        progressive lenses.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp class=\\\"p1\\\"\u003eOnce you have your PD, you can upload your photo to the Frame Fit tool and begin trying on glasses. The Frame Fit\\n        tool allows you to see exactly what the glasses look like on you and how well they fit the size and shape of\\n        your face. If you don’t have your PD, you can find out how to measure it \u003ca href=\\\"/measuring-pd-infographic\\\"\\n            target=\\\"_blank;\\\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.reviews.ratingSnapshotTitle\":\"Rating Snapshot\",\"pdp.reviews.recommendCountSingular\":\"{{count}} of {{total}} customer recommend\",\"pdp.reviews.newestFirst\":\"Newest\",\"pdp.reviews.showLess\":\"Show less\",\"pdp.reviews.mostHelpfulFirst\":\"Most helpful\",\"pdp.tabs.details.prescriptionRange.description\":\"Additional cost for PDs outside this range\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.prism\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"tw-gap-10 tw-flex tw-flex-col\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003ePrism is the prismatic power used to correct vision displacement, like double vision. Most eyeglass prescriptions\\n        do not have prism correction. Prism is a measure in prism diopters.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003eA prescription with prism prescription will have two values per eye. Zenni is able to accommodate prism\\n        corrections with a range of 0.25 to 5.00 diopters in any direction or combination of directions. If you have a\\n        combination of the horizontal and vertical prism, the prism input may be more limited. Base Direction is usually\\n        written as BU for Base Up, BD for Base Down, BI for Base In, and BO for Base Out.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003eIf you do not have prism correction in your prescription, do not include prism values since it will negatively\\n        affect your vision.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003ePrism corrections are available only for single-vision prescriptions, not bifocals or progressives.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.reviews.aiNote\":\"This summary was generated by AI to help you quickly understand customer feedback.\",\"pdp.reviews.helpful\":\"Was this review helpful?\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.cyl\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"tw-gap-10 tw-flex tw-flex-col\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n        CYL, for Cylinder, refers to the strength of the correction for the astigmatism in the eye. It can be\\n        either positive or negative. If there is a CYL value on an eye, there \u003cstrong\u003emust\u003c/strong\u003e be\\n        an Axis value on that eye.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n        If \\\"\u003cstrong\u003eDS\u003c/strong\u003e\\\" or \\\"\u003cstrong\u003eSPH\u003c/strong\u003e\\\" or \\\"spherical\\\" is noted in the CYL space on your\\n        prescription, you have no astigmatism in that eye. In that case, enter \u003cstrong\u003e0.00 \u003c/strong\u003ein both\\n        the CYL and Axis.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n        \u003cstrong\u003eOD-CYL\u003c/strong\u003e is cylinder correction for your \u003cstrong\u003eright\u003c/strong\u003e eye.\u003cbr/\u003e\\n        \u003cstrong\u003eOS-CYL\u003c/strong\u003e is cylinder correction for your \u003cstrong\u003eleft\u003c/strong\u003e eye.\\n    \u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.reviews.overallRatingTitle\":\"Overall Rating\",\"pdp.reviews.customerReviews\":\"Customer Reviews\",\"pdp.reviews.recommendCount\":\"{{count}} of {{total}} customers recommend\",\"pdp.relatedSku.title\":\"Customers also bought\",\"pdp.reviews.readMore\":\"Read more\",\"pdp.reviews.lowestRatingFirst\":\"Lowest rating\",\"pdp.reviews.beTheFirstToWriteAReview\":\"Be the first to share your experience and help others find their perfect pair! \",\"pdp.reviews.stars\":\"stars\",\"pdp.reviews.extraTitle\":\"View all photos\",\"pdp.reviews.customerSay\":\"Customers are saying...\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.progressiveOption\":\"$4c\",\"pdp.reviews.star\":\"star\",\"pdp.reviews.highestRatingFirst\":\"Highest rating\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.nvAdd\":\"\u003cdiv\u003e\\n    Sometimes seen on your prescription as \\\"\u003cstrong\u003eNV, ADD, Near, Reading, \u003c/strong\u003eor\u003cstrong\u003e Reading\\n        Addition\u003c/strong\u003e.\\\"  \\\"NV\\\" stands for \\\"Near-Vision.\\\"  This number indicates the additional\\n    magnification that is added to the distance prescription to get the reading portion of the lens in a multi-focal\\n    prescription.  We display a single NV-ADD field since it is \u003cstrong\u003ealmost always the same value for\\n        both eyes.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.reviews.title\":\"Customer Photos\",\"pdp.reviews.allMediaTitle\":\"Reviews with images\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.axis\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"tw-gap-10 tw-flex tw-flex-col\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n        AXS, or Axis, refers to the angle of the correction for the astigmatism in the eye (if one exists) from 1 to\\n        180.  If there is an Axis value on an eye, there \u003cstrong\u003emust\u003c/strong\u003e be a CYL (Cylinder) value\\n        on that eye. If there is \u003cstrong\u003eno\u003c/strong\u003e Cylinder value or if the value is zero, the OD Axis\\n        value is entered as \u003cstrong\u003e0.00\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n        The Axis value is usually written as 3 digits, which means if your Axis value is 5, it is often written as 005.\\n        This Axis value is still 5, regardless of how it is displayed.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp\u003e\\n        \u003cstrong\u003eOD Axis\u003c/strong\u003e is Axis correction for your \u003cstrong\u003eright \u003c/strong\u003eeye.\u003cbr /\u003e\\n        \u003cstrong\u003eOS Axis\u003c/strong\u003e is Axis correction for your \u003cstrong\u003eleft \u003c/strong\u003eeye.\\n    \u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.reviews.averageRatingsTitle\":\"Average Ratings\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.prescriptionType\":\"$4d\",\"pdp.sports.entrypoints.config\":\"$4e\",\"account.prescription.form.tooltipContent.sph\":\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"tw-gap-10 tw-flex tw-flex-col\\\"\u003e\\n    \u003cp class=\\\"p1\\\"\u003e\\n        SPH, for Spherical, refers to the refractive correction in the prescription. Minus (-) are for near\\n        sightedness, and Plus (+) values are for far sightedness. If \\\"\u003cstrong\u003ePL\u003c/strong\u003e\\\" or\\n        \\\"\u003cstrong\u003ePlano\u003c/strong\u003e\\\" is written for the either SPH value on your prescription, you should select a value of\\n        0.00.\u003c/p\u003e\\n    \u003cp class=\\\"p1\\\"\u003e\\n        \u003cstrong\u003eOD-SPH\u003c/strong\u003e is spherical correction for your \u003cstrong\u003eright\u003c/strong\u003e eye.\u003cbr /\u003e\\n        \u003cstrong\u003eOS-SPH\u003c/strong\u003e is spherical correction for your \u003cstrong\u003eleft\u003c/strong\u003e eye.\\n    \u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/div\u003e\",\"pdp.vr.aboutVRLenses\":\"Have questions about VR lenses? \u003ca href=\\\"/vr-prescription-lenses-meta-quest-3\\\" class=\\\"tw-cursor-pointer tw-text-black tw-underline hover:tw-text-gray-700 hover:tw-no-underline\\\"\u003eLearn more\u003c/a\u003e\",\"pdp.reviews.faceShape\":\"Face Shape\",\"pdp.reviews.verified\":\"Verified customer\",\"plp.filter.defaultOpen.list\":\"[\\\"Filter by\\\"]\",\"global.pdp.flashSaleTitle\":\"Claim $1 Flash Sale deal by spending $24 on lenses\",\"err.frame.fullrim.rx.strong\":\"Your prescription is too strong for this frame.\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4f\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"id\":\"glasseson\"}],[\"$\",\"$L50\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"segmentPath\":[\"children\"],\"error\":\"$51\",\"errorStyles\":[],\"errorScripts\":[],\"template\":[\